WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.560
The school assigns suction depth and tube-displacement learning. The goal is to reason safely through airway danger, not to memorize a universal tube-change recipe.
学校指定吸引深度及导管移位学习。目标是安全推理气道危险，而非背通用换管处方。

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:21.576
Start with responsiveness, effective breathing and immediate ventilation needs. A long device inventory must not delay support for apnea or severe distress.
应先看反应、有效呼吸及即时通气需要。呼吸暂停或重度窘迫时，不能因长清点器械而延误支持。

00:00:21.576 --> 00:00:29.520
Ask the patient or trained caregiver what is normal, where the emergency plan is and which equipment is personal to this airway.
需问患者或受训照护者其平常状态、急救方案位置，以及哪些器械专属此气道。

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:38.736
This lesson prepares for a supervised school station. It does not certify suctioning or authorize routine replacement of a tracheostomy tube.
本课为监督下学校站点作准备；不认证吸引，也不授权常规更换气切导管。

00:00:38.736 --> 00:00:48.048
A tracheostomy is an opening into the trachea. The patient may have variable upper-airway patency depending on the indication and anatomy.
气管切开是通向气管的开口。依适应症及解剖，患者上气道通畅性可能不同。

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:57.216
After total laryngectomy, the airway is separated from the mouth and nose. Ventilation through the face may not reach the lungs.
全喉切除后气道与口鼻分离，经面部通气可能无法进入肺。

00:00:57.216 --> 00:01:04.752
A cricothyrotomy is created at a different anatomical site and has different equipment and training requirements.
环甲膜切开位于不同解剖部位，器械及训练要求也不同。

00:01:04.752 --> 00:01:16.536
Ask about the operation, device and usual breathing route; look for reliable records or a patient-specific plan. Never label an airway from a quick visual assumption alone.
应询问手术、器械及平时呼吸路径，并查可靠记录或个体方案。绝不能仅凭快速目视猜定气道类型。

00:01:16.536 --> 00:01:26.880
Some tracheostomy patients can breathe around the tube and through the upper airway; others cannot. Anatomy may also change with swelling or illness.
部分气切患者可绕管并经上气道呼吸，另一些不能；肿胀或疾病也可改变解剖状况。

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:36.072
A patient with total laryngectomy depends on the stoma for ventilation. Face-mask oxygen alone does not solve a blocked stoma.
全喉切除患者依赖造口通气；仅给面罩氧不能解决造口阻塞。

00:01:36.072 --> 00:01:43.008
A speaking valve, cap, cuff, upper-airway obstruction and altered anatomy all affect how air moves.
发声阀、封帽、套囊、上气道阻塞及解剖变化都会影响气流。

00:01:43.008 --> 00:01:51.576
Observe chest movement, airflow and response to support; do not assume that a visible stoma proves the tube is patent.
应观察胸廓起伏、气流及支持反应；不能因看见造口就认定导管通畅。

00:01:51.576 --> 00:02:01.056
Not every tracheostomy has an inner cannula, and designs differ. Identify the actual model before attempting to remove any component.
并非每根气切管都有内套管，设计亦有差异。拆卸任何部件前，需识别真实型号。

00:02:01.056 --> 00:02:10.608
The cuff is not a one-way valve and does not reliably prevent aspiration. Its status affects ventilation, leakage and comfort.
套囊不是单向阀，也不能可靠防误吸；其状态会影响通气、漏气及舒适度。

00:02:10.608 --> 00:02:20.952
A removed inner cannula may also remove the standard ventilation connector on some devices. Follow the actual device design and emergency plan.
部分器械拆下内套管也会失去标准通气接头；需遵循真实器械设计及急救方案。

00:02:20.952 --> 00:02:32.760
Do not inflate, deflate or remove a cuff simply because a textbook lists that step. The indication, training, device and current local procedure must all match.
不能仅因教材列有步骤就充气、放气或拆套囊；适应症、训练、器械及现行当地规程都必须相符。

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:41.688
The obstruction may be at a humidification filter, speaking valve, cap, connector or oxygen tubing rather than deep in the airway.
阻塞可能在加湿过滤器、发声阀、封帽、接头或氧管，而非气道深部。

00:02:41.688 --> 00:02:51.024
Ask the patient or caregiver what is normally attached and what was recently changed. A device may be essential to a home ventilator setup.
需问患者或照护者平常连接什么、最近有何变化；器械可能是家庭呼吸机设置的必要部分。

00:02:51.024 --> 00:02:58.896
Check visible connections, kinks and equipment function without disconnecting a ventilator or device beyond your training.
可查可见接口、折弯及器械功能，但不能超训练断开呼吸机或装置。

00:02:58.896 --> 00:03:06.480
Remove an attachment only when its purpose is understood and the patient-specific plan or trained procedure supports it.
仅当理解附件用途且个体方案或受训规程允许时才拆。

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:17.640
Assess airway and breathing immediately. Look for poor chest rise, increased effort, noisy airflow, cyanosis or a falling level of responsiveness.
需立即评估气道呼吸，观察胸廓起伏差、用力增加、气流异常、发绀或反应下降。

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:26.784
Supplemental oxygen does not correct ineffective ventilation. Use the appropriate trained support pathway when breaths are inadequate.
补充氧不能纠正无效通气；呼吸不足时应依适当受训支持路径。

00:03:26.784 --> 00:03:36.864
Use monitoring as an aid, not a substitute for the patient. A normal-looking number does not overrule a deteriorating level of effort or consciousness.
监测是辅助，不替代患者本身。看似正常数字不能推翻呼吸用力或意识恶化。

00:03:36.864 --> 00:03:44.160
Ask another team member to prepare suction and the patient-specific backup equipment while primary support continues.
维持主要支持时，可让另一名队员准备吸引器及患者专属备用器械。

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:53.904
Ask the patient directly where possible. Some people with a tracheostomy communicate by voice, writing, gesture or an assistive device.
可行时应直接询问患者；气切者可用声音、书写、手势或辅助装置沟通。

00:03:53.904 --> 00:04:03.816
A trained caregiver may know the baseline, exact tube model, usual suction depth and the home emergency plan. Confirm, do not assume.
受训照护者可能知道基线、准确管型、平常吸引深度及家庭急救方案；应核实，不能默认。

00:04:03.816 --> 00:04:11.016
Locate the personal emergency kit and check that the identified equipment is actually available and compatible.
需找到个人急救包，并核对所需器械确实存在且兼容。

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:20.472
Separate the first noticed change from the presumed cause. The family may report a plug, but the patient still needs an independent airway assessment.
需区分最先察觉的变化与推测病因；家属可报告黏液栓，但患者仍需独立气道评估。

00:04:20.472 --> 00:04:29.184
Check the suction source and tubing before the procedure. A powered unit that is not charged or connected is not a working backup.
操作前需检查吸引器及管路；没电或未连接的主机不是可用备用。

00:04:29.184 --> 00:04:39.264
Select the catheter using the actual tube dimensions and applicable training guidance. A smaller catheter is not automatically correct for every tube.
应按真实导管尺寸及适用训练指引选吸痰管；较小规格并非对所有导管都自动正确。

00:04:39.264 --> 00:04:50.184
Use a premeasured tube-limited insertion depth or the patient-specific written depth. Never estimate an unseen carina distance from a generic nursing diagram.
应采用预先测量的限管深度或患者书面个体深度；不能按通用护理图估算不可见隆嵴距离。

00:04:50.184 --> 00:05:00.120
Have oxygenation, monitoring and a plan for deterioration available. The patient can desaturate or become bradycardic during an airway procedure.
需备妥氧合、监测及恶化方案；气道操作期间患者可能脱饱和或心动过缓。

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:09.360
Suction may be considered when secretions are visible, audible or associated with impaired ventilation and the patient cannot clear them effectively.
当分泌物可见、可闻，或伴通气受损且患者不能有效清除时，可考虑吸引。

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:19.224
A trained patient may recognize a familiar mucus-plug pattern early. Treat that history seriously while independently confirming current findings.
受训患者可能及早认出熟悉的黏液栓表现；应重视其描述，同时独立核实当前表现。

00:05:19.224 --> 00:05:31.368
Routine suction can cause distress, mucosal trauma, bleeding, bronchospasm or hypoxia. A schedule alone is not enough reason to perform it in an emergency scene.
常规吸引可引起痛苦、黏膜损伤、出血、支气管痉挛或低氧；急救现场仅凭计划时间不足以操作。

00:05:31.368 --> 00:05:39.744
Explain the procedure, prepare the equipment and oxygenation plan, and use the least invasive effective action allowed by training.
需解释操作、准备器械及氧合计划，并采用训练允许的有效且尽量低侵入动作。

00:05:39.744 --> 00:05:50.280
The school specifically names suction depth. The safest transferable concept is to measure the actual tube or use a current patient-specific depth plan before insertion.
学校特别要求吸引深度。最可迁移的安全原则是插入前测量真实导管，或依现行患者个体深度方案。

00:05:50.280 --> 00:06:00.048
Mark the catheter at the measured endpoint so the operator can see the stopping limit. Do not push to resistance and then withdraw by a guessed amount.
应在测定终点标记吸痰管，让操作者看见停止界限；不能推到阻力处再凭猜测回退。

00:06:00.048 --> 00:06:11.376
Advance gently without applying suction during insertion. If the catheter does not pass to the expected tube-limited depth, stop and reassess obstruction or displacement.
送入时应轻柔且不吸引；若未能达到预期限管深度，应停止并重评阻塞或移位。

00:06:11.376 --> 00:06:19.872
A fixed number from an unrelated adult or nursing source is not a universal depth for a child, different tube or altered stoma.
无关成人或护理来源的固定数字，不是儿童、不同管型或改变造口的通用深度。

00:06:19.872 --> 00:06:29.184
Use the exact technique taught for the actual device and school station. This is a supervised skill, not a procedure to improvise from a slide.
应使用真实器械及学校站点教授的准确技术。这是监督技能，不应按课件自行发明。

00:06:29.184 --> 00:06:37.728
Do not apply continuous suction while advancing. Advance only to the visible depth mark and do not force through resistance.
送入时不能持续吸引；仅送至可见深度标记，遇阻不强行推进。

00:06:37.728 --> 00:06:46.656
Apply suction during withdrawal if that is the station procedure. Keep the pass short and maintain observation of the patient throughout.
若站点流程如此，应在退出时吸引；单次应短，并持续观察患者。

00:06:46.656 --> 00:06:55.536
Reoxygenate and reassess between passes. Repeated attempts without a new assessment can worsen hypoxia and cause injury.
两次吸引间应恢复氧合并复评；未重评便连续尝试可能加重低氧及损伤。

00:06:55.536 --> 00:07:05.856
After the pass, compare the same signs used before it: work of breathing, chest movement, air entry, oxygenation and alertness.
吸引后需比较操作前相同体征：呼吸功、胸廓活动、进气、氧合及觉醒。

00:07:05.856 --> 00:07:15.096
If no secretion is recovered or breathing does not improve, do not assume the airway is clear. Recheck the device and consider other causes.
若无分泌物或呼吸未改善，不能认定气道已通；应重查器械并考虑其他病因。

00:07:15.096 --> 00:07:22.248
If the patient deteriorates, stop the procedure and move to the trained airway-support and escalation plan.
若患者恶化，应停止操作并转入受训气道支持及升级方案。

00:07:22.248 --> 00:07:33.264
Record the reason for suction, measured insertion limit, response and any complication. Avoid recording a routine action when the depth or response is unknown.
需记录吸引原因、测定插入界限、反应及并发情况；深度或反应未知时不能记成常规步骤已完成。

00:07:33.264 --> 00:07:43.896
Failure to pass can reflect a blocked tube, displaced tube, kink, secretions or incorrect equipment. It is not proof of only one cause.
无法送入可能是阻塞、移位、折弯、分泌物或器械不符，并非只证明一种原因。

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:53.808
Stop rather than force the catheter. Force can injure tissue or create a false passage, especially when the tract is new or the tube is displaced.
应停止，不可强推；强行可能损伤组织或造成假道，新造口或导管移位时尤其危险。

00:07:53.808 --> 00:08:04.104
Check only those removable parts you are trained and authorized to handle. A missing connector or partially displaced outer tube can be mistaken for obstruction.
只能检查受训且获准处理的可拆部件；缺少接头或外管部分移位可能被误当阻塞。

00:08:04.104 --> 00:08:14.352
Prioritize adequate ventilation, request advanced assistance and transport. Do not spend repeated minutes attempting an unapproved tube change.
应优先保证通气、请求高级协助并运输；不能反复花分钟尝试未获准换管。

00:08:14.352 --> 00:08:24.312
A recently created stoma may not have a stable tract. Replacing a tube through a fresh or uncertain opening can create a false passage.
新造口可能尚无稳定通道；通过新鲜或不确定开口换管可能形成假道。

00:08:24.312 --> 00:08:34.440
Watch for a changed flange position, loss of expected airflow, leak, subcutaneous air or sudden distress after movement or coughing.
需注意固定翼位置变化、预期气流消失、漏气、皮下气或移动咳嗽后突然窘迫。

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:42.432
Do not blindly push a displaced tube back. Stop and use the patient-specific emergency plan with trained assistance.
导管移位时不可盲目推回；应停下并在受训协助下采用患者急救方案。

00:08:42.432 --> 00:08:54.144
The actual response depends on anatomy, stoma age, device, training, service scope and patient response; this lesson cannot substitute for that authorized algorithm.
实际应对取决于解剖、造口年龄、器械、训练、服务范围及患者反应；本课不能替代获准算法。

00:08:54.144 --> 00:09:02.952
A face mask may help a person with a tracheostomy if the upper airway remains patent; it may fail when the upper route is obstructed.
若上气道仍通，面罩可能帮助气切患者；上路阻塞时则可能无效。

00:09:02.952 --> 00:09:10.344
For total laryngectomy, ventilation must be directed to the stoma because the upper airway is disconnected.
全喉切除者因上气道断开，通气须针对造口。

00:09:10.344 --> 00:09:19.224
Cuff inflation, deflation and tube removal change the ventilation route and require the actual device plan and qualified operator.
套囊充放及导管拆除会改变通气路径，须依真实器械方案及合格操作者。

00:09:19.224 --> 00:09:30.096
Assess visible chest movement and air leak with every attempt. Do not interpret a tight mask seal or a numerical reading as proof of effective ventilation.
每次尝试均需评估可见胸廓活动及漏气；面罩贴合或数字读数不能证明有效通气。

00:09:30.096 --> 00:09:37.656
DOPE can help structure troubleshooting when a ventilated patient suddenly worsens. It is a reminder list, not a diagnosis.
患者通气时突然恶化，可用DOPE组织排查；它是提醒列表，不是诊断。

00:09:37.656 --> 00:09:45.816
Check displacement and obstruction while support continues. Examine connections and equipment without losing the airway.
维持支持时查移位及阻塞，并检查连接器械，不能丢失气道控制。

00:09:45.816 --> 00:09:54.696
Pneumothorax and other clinical causes still require assessment in context. A tracheostomy does not make every decline a tube fault.
气胸及其他临床原因仍需结合情境评估；气切不代表每次恶化都是导管故障。

00:09:54.696 --> 00:10:04.704
Use the list to prompt the next check, then reassess whether the patient improves. A memorable mnemonic is not a substitute for a current service pathway.
可用口诀提示下一核查，再复评患者是否改善；好记口诀不能替代现行服务路径。

00:10:04.704 --> 00:10:14.472
A five-year-old with an established tracheostomy becomes less interactive. The caregiver reports that breathing has become noisy over several minutes.
一名5岁气切儿童互动减少；照护者报告数分钟内呼吸变得嘈杂。

00:10:14.472 --> 00:10:24.768
The crew sees secretions at the opening and checks chest rise, oxygen equipment and the patient-specific plan. One member maintains the primary assessment.
救护组见开口处有分泌物，检查胸廓起伏、氧设备及个体方案；一人维持主要评估。

00:10:24.768 --> 00:10:37.512
For the classroom branch, the station supervisor supplies the measured suction depth and appropriate catheter. The learner demonstrates a brief, gentle, marked-depth pass on a manikin.
课堂分支中，站点教师提供测量深度及适配吸痰管；学员在模型上示范短暂、轻柔、带标记深度的操作。

00:10:37.512 --> 00:10:48.192
The mannequin improves only after a small secretion is cleared. State the reassessment findings, what would trigger escalation and what you would report to the receiving team.
模型仅在清除少量分泌物后改善；学员需说明复评发现、升级触发点及向接收团队报告内容。

00:10:48.192 --> 00:10:55.008
Report whether the patient normally uses the stoma, mouth or both for breathing and how they usually communicate.
需报告患者平时经造口、口鼻或两者呼吸，以及惯用沟通方式。

00:10:55.008 --> 00:11:03.432
Give the time of change, witnessed symptoms and relevant device event. Distinguish direct observation from caregiver report.
应交代变化时刻、目击症状及器械事件，并区分亲见与照护者转述。

00:11:03.432 --> 00:11:13.728
Describe the equipment checked, whether a catheter passed, the measured depth used and the response. Do not collapse the sequence to “suctioned, stable.”
需说明检查器械、吸痰管是否通过、实测深度及反应；不能只写“已吸引，稳定”。

00:11:13.728 --> 00:11:21.912
Include the patient-specific plan, caregiver expertise, equipment sent with the patient and any requested advanced follow-up.
需交代个体方案、照护者经验、随患者携带器械及请求的高级后续处理。

00:11:21.912 --> 00:11:32.472
The assigned nursing chapters discuss specimen collection, assessment and tube care. Those chapters are educational sources, not paramedic scope documents.
指定护理章节介绍标本、评估及导管照护，但它们是教学资料，不是救护员执业范围文件。

00:11:32.472 --> 00:11:42.912
Some emergency tube changes are designed for specifically trained family caregivers with a personal plan. That does not authorize an untrained responder to imitate them.
部分急救换管是为有个体方案的特定受训家属设计；不授权未受训人员模仿。

00:11:42.912 --> 00:11:53.472
Use the actual BC service procedure, school skill sheet, device directions and instructor when the required depth, pressure or route is not stated here.
如本课未给出所需深度、压力或路径，应使用真实BC服务程序、学校技能表、器械说明及教师指导。

00:11:53.472 --> 00:12:02.808
Do not use this slide deck as a bedside operational checklist. The patient and local protocol take priority over a generic classroom aid.
不能把本课件当床旁操作检查表；患者及当地现行规程优先于通用课堂辅助。

00:12:02.808 --> 00:12:09.528
First state the airway anatomy and normal route, using confirmed history rather than guessing from the stoma.
首先依据已核实病史说明气道解剖及平常路径，不能只凭造口猜测。

00:12:09.528 --> 00:12:18.576
Next name the observed problem and immediate support need. Avoid diagnosing a mucus plug just because the caregiver used that phrase.
再指出实际观察到的问题及即时支持需要；不能因照护者用了黏液栓一词就直接确诊。

00:12:18.576 --> 00:12:27.264
If suction is indicated, explain how the actual depth limit is obtained and how you will stop if resistance or deterioration occurs.
若需吸引，应解释真实深度界限如何取得，以及遇阻或恶化时如何停止。

00:12:27.264 --> 00:12:36.384
Finally name the trained clinician, local service pathway and escalation resource. If one is missing, do not invent the missing permission.
最后需指出受训临床人员、当地服务路径及升级资源；缺少任何一项都不能臆造授权。
